'''''Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide''''' is a [[canon]] reference book written by [[Daniel Wallace]] that was released on [[November 13]], [[2018]].

==Publisher's summary==
''Recovered from a strong box on the ''Millennium Falcon'', the ''Smuggler's Guide'' traces its own extraordinary journey through such notorious characters as Maz Kanata, Hondo Ohnaka, Dryden Vos, Lando Calrissian, and Han Solo. Explore previously unknown details about the underhanded dealings of the galaxy's underworld. What secrets will you discover in these storied pages?''

==Development==
Although initially slated for an [[October 30]], [[2018]]<ref name="In This Life for Good">{{SW|url=news/smugglers-guide-dan-wallace|text=When You Read the New Book ''Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide'', You're in This Life for Good}}</ref> release, the deluxe edition of ''Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide'' was pushed back to [[November 13]], 2018.<ref name="Smugglers Guide Amazon" /> When a fan asked the reason for the delay, author [[Daniel Wallace]] cited logistical issues in international shipping, but said he expected the issue to be resolved soon.<ref name="Wallace tweet">{{Twitter|danwall88|status/1058133304271142912|[[Daniel Wallace]]|quote=Hi, have been checking into this. Apparently there were logistical issues with intl shipping but should start going out soon}}</ref>

==Continuity==
*The names of the [[Rimma Trade Route]] and [[Corellian Trade Spine]] are erroneously swapped in the map on page 6, as confirmed by Daniel Wallace on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]].<ref name="Hyperlance Tweet">{{Twitter|danwall88|status/1076886688125935616|[[Daniel Wallace]]|quote=Definitely not intentional. Apologies, I must have missed that and you're actually the first one to point it out}} &mdash; [[Daniel Wallace]] confirms that the names of the [[Corellian Trade Spine]] and [[Rimma Trade Route]] are not supposed to be swapped in ''Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide''.</ref> Also on page 6, [[Kashyyyk]] is misspelled as "Kashyyk," and in the book's [[2019]] and [[2021]] editions (but not the 2018 one), all the [[hyperspace route]]s on that page are erroneously shifted left of their correct position.
*On page 68, valachord is seemingly misspelled as 'vanachord' as stated by [[Matt Martin]].<ref name="Valachord Tweet">{{Twitter|missingwords|status/1333237159684308992|[[Matt Martin]]|quote=Sounds like a typo. I'll let them know to adjust it if it gets reprinted. What page is it on?}} &mdash; [[Matt Martin]] indicates that the item valachord is most likely misspelled as vanachord in ''Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide''.</ref>
*On page 114, the ''[[Graceful Promising]]'' is spelled as ''Grateful Promising'' despite the former spelling appearing on pages 7 and 113.
*On page 137, the ''[[Meson Martinet]]'' is incorrectly depicted as an [[XS stock light freighter]].

